call.aspx"},{"c":"RYN 2018 Q3","e":"ryn","d":"2018-11-01","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Douglas Long","x":"The reduction in price compared to both periods was influenced by general shift in volume from the East Coast to the Gulf states combined with the impact of China tariffs on export prices.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/11/01/rayonier-inc-ryn-q3-2018-earnings-conference-call.aspx"},{"c":"RYN 2018 Q3","e":"ryn","d":"2018-11-01","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"David Nunes","x":"So we would-I think by shipping and we are seeing price increase there, but this kind of new influx of shipping capacity, we are seeing some prices come down in our shipping rates also in this quarter.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/11/01/rayonier-inc-ryn-q3-2018-earnings-conference-call.aspx"},{"c":"RYN 2018 Q3","e":"ryn","d":"2018-11-01","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Mark McHugh","x":"And as I mentioned, we're seeing some cost savings on shipping.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/11/01/rayonier-inc-ryn-q3-2018-earnings-conference-call.aspx"},{"c":"RYN 2019 Q2","e":"ryn","d":"2019-08-08","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"David Nunes","x":"Following the significant decline in pricing from the third quarter of last year when the trade war heated up, pricing has been relatively stable over the last three quarters.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/08/09/rayonier-ryn-q2-2019-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"RYN 2019 Q2","e":"ryn","d":"2019-08-08","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"David Nunes","x":"And a case in point, earlier in the year, there was the expectation that tariffs in the Northwest would go from the current 5% to something in the 20% range.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/08/09/rayonier-ryn-q2-2019-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"RYN 2019 Q2","e":"ryn","d":"2019-08-08","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Mark McHugh","x":"As noted in our earnings release, based on the lingering U.S.-China trade dispute and its associated market impacts, we are lowering our full-year guidance.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/08/09/rayonier-ryn-q2-2019-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"RYN 2019 Q2","e":"ryn","d":"2019-08-08","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Mark McHugh","x":"Taking these factors together, we're reducing our outlook for full-year adjusted EBITDA in our Pacific Northwest timber segment to $13 million to $16 million.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/08/09/rayonier-ryn-q2-2019-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"RYN 2019 Q3","e":"ryn","d":"2019-10-31","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Doug Long","x":"The decline in pricing compared to both prior periods was primarily due to weaker export and domestic demand resulting from continued Chinese tariffs on southern yellow pine logs coupled with an increase in tariffs on southern yellow pine lumber, which impacted domestic production.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/11/01/rayonier-ryn-q3-2019-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"RYN 2019 Q3","e":"ryn","d":"2019-10-31","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Doug Long","x":"…that significant decrease from marginal suppliers such as South America, and as I mentioned, the tariff constraints in U.S. South, 50% reduction in block trains from Europe on the One Belt's Road initiative from 300 to 150 per month trailing number And that significant increase in plywood…","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/11/01/rayonier-ryn-q3-2019-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"RYN 2019 Q4","e":"ryn","d":"2020-02-06","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"David Nunes","x":"This result represents a significant decline from the prior year as log export volumes and log prices declined dramatically following the implementation tariffs by China in late 2018.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/02/07/rayonier-ryn-q4-2019-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"RYN 2019 Q4","e":"ryn","d":"2020-02-06","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Doug Long","x":"Prices remain flat in the course of the year as a result of the continued tariffs on log exports in China, and competition from European salvage timber.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/02/07/rayonier-ryn-q4-2019-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"RYN 2019 Q4","e":"ryn","d":"2020-02-06","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Mark McHugh","x":"…that top line volatility, that 10% swing in pricing has a much more pronounced effect on your bottom line than it does in say the South, where if you're kind of measuring price moves off of stumpage revenue, that stumpage revenue is 80-plus percent EBITDA margin in terms of the pass-through.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/02/07/rayonier-ryn-q4-2019-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"RYN 2019 Q4","e":"ryn","d":"2020-02-06","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Mark McHugh","x":"And so we ended up having to cut our guidance pretty significantly midyear for the Pacific Northwest.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/02/07/rayonier-ryn-q4-2019-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"RYN 2020 Q1","e":"ryn","d":"2020-04-30","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Doug Long","x":"Then toward the end of the quarter, demand for export timber picked up as China tariffs were waived.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/05/04/rayonier-ryn-q1-2020-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"RYN 2020 Q1","e":"ryn","d":"2020-04-30","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Randy Toth","x":"And just to clarify, these Chinese tariff waivers, are those just on logs coming out of the PAC northwest or does that cover southern timberland as well?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/05/04/rayonier-ryn-q1-2020-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"RYN 2020 Q1","e":"ryn","d":"2020-04-30","l":"guidance","r":"analyst","s":"Paul Quinn","x":"I'm not surprised with the reduced guidance.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/05/04/rayonier-ryn-q1-2020-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"RYN 2020 Q4","e":"ryn","d":"2021-02-04","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Salvator Tiano","x":"But, firstly, how does this compare essentially to where you were before China imposed the tariffs on the U.S. when things were growing at a very high rate as well?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/02/04/rayonier-inc-ryn-q4-2020-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"RYN 2020 Q4","e":"ryn","d":"2021-02-04","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Douglas M. Long","x":"We were -- we've just gotten started in the export markets before the tariffs went in, in June of 2018.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/02/04/rayonier-inc-ryn-q4-2020-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"RYN 2020 Q4","e":"ryn","d":"2021-02-04","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Douglas M. Long","x":"Pricing increases tend to be a straight pass-through to the bottom line; whereas the volume increases, you're obviously getting kind of that marginal contribution from the incremental tons.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/02/04/rayonier-inc-ryn-q4-2020-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"RYN 2020 Q4","e":"ryn","d":"2021-02-04","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Douglas M. Long","x":"So, it has had some impact but overall we're seeing a price increase in all the markets.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/02/04/rayonier-inc-ryn-q4-2020-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"RYN 2021 Q1","e":"ryn","d":"2021-05-06","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Douglas M. Long","x":"And the Indian customers took advantage of that Australia-China trade war arbitrage opportunity, and so they were seeking logs and getting those logs that were supposed to go to China that then went to India.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/05/06/rayonier-inc-ryn-q1-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"RYN 2021 Q1","e":"ryn","d":"2021-05-06","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"David L. Nunes","x":"John, keep in mind that this started back in 2007 when the Russian government put in place an export tariff.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/05/06/rayonier-inc-ryn-q1-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"RYN 2021 Q1","e":"ryn","d":"2021-05-06","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Douglas M. Long","x":"And with this cost, our end-product customers are also seeing that increase, and so they're working to pass that on to their end products.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/05/06/rayonier-inc-ryn-q1-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"RYN 2021 Q2","e":"ryn","d":"2021-08-05","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Doug Long","x":"So we're very pleased with the outcome so far, but I kind of talk one more general terms and as of May US, South Southern Yellow Pine log exports have recovered to the 200,000 cubic meters per month achieved prior to the tariffs implant in 2018.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/08/05/rayonier-inc-ryn-q2-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"RYN 2021 Q2","e":"ryn","d":"2021-08-05","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"John Babcock","x":"I mean if that does have some pass-through effect into log prices how sustainable would that increase there or would that just be something that's variable based on freight rates?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/08/05/rayonier-inc-ryn-q2-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"RYN 2021 Q2","e":"ryn","d":"2021-08-05","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Dave Nunes","x":"But also and then just with the integration of Pope Resources and sort of rightsizing the overall corporate, we're still working through some of that.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/08/05/rayonier-inc-ryn-q2-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"RYN 2021 Q2","e":"ryn","d":"2021-08-05","l":"guidance","r":"analyst","s":"Paul Quinn","x":"Just strong results in, I'd like to see the increased guidance, one of the areas that would also saw an increase in corporate costs but what is that increase related to?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/08/05/rayonier-inc-ryn-q2-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"RYN 2021 Q2","e":"ryn","d":"2021-08-05","l":"guidance","r":"unknown","s":"Unidentified Participant","x":"Thanks, that's helpful and then just with regards to raise guidance, can you talk about what the biggest swing factors that could get you to maybe the high or low end of the range, is it fair to say that China demand maybe New Zealand or the biggest sources of variability or other factors that we…","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/08/05/rayonier-inc-ryn-q2-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"RYN 2021 Q3","e":"ryn","d":"2021-11-04","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Douglas M. Long","x":"And so as we're seeing the cost increase, we're off seeing price increases.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/11/04/rayonier-inc-ryn-q3-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"RYN 2025 Q2","e":"ryn","d":"2025-08-07","l":"ai_spend","r":"management","s":"Mark McHugh","x":"The rapid deployment of AI and the data centers needed to support this technology are driving significant growth in energy demand, and utility solar remains poised to play a major role in meeting the need for cost-effective renewable energy.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2025/08/07/rayonier-ryn-q2-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"RYN 2025 Q2","e":"ryn","d":"2025-08-07","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Doug Long","x":"Pulpwood net stumpage pricing was 25% lower than the prior year quarter at roughly $13 per ton, driven by the continued impact of salvage volume on the market, softer demand from pulp mills due to maintenance outages and tariff uncertainty, and an unfavorable shift in geographic mix.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2025/08/07/rayonier-ryn-q2-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"RYN 2025 Q2","e":"ryn","d":"2025-08-07","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Doug Long","x":"Further, if new tariffs are implemented on lumber and other wood products under the Section 232 investigation that began in March, this would likely serve as an additional catalyst to drive both lumber prices and U.S. lumber production higher, which should in turn bolster sawtimber prices in the…","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2025/08/07/rayonier-ryn-q2-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"RYN 2025 Q2","e":"ryn","d":"2025-08-07","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"Anthony Pettinari","x":"So their permitting technology action plan administration is aiming to see that the class six wells get permitted within two years, and that's through promoting state primacy and also streamlining regulatory reviews.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2025/08/07/rayonier-ryn-q2-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"RYN 2025 Q3","e":"ryn","d":"2025-11-06","l":"ai_spend","r":"management","s":"Mark McHugh","x":"In particular, the substantial capital that continues to flow into AI and data center infrastructure is driving significant growth in energy demand and utility solar remains poised to play a major role in meeting the need for cost-effective renewable energy.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/02/12/rayonier-ryn-q3-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"RYN 2025 Q3","e":"ryn","d":"2025-11-06","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Douglas Long","x":"…we expect U.S. lumber production to eventually ramp up in response to higher duties on Canadian lumber imports, the recently announced Section 232 tariffs of 10% on all softwood lumber imports and the prospect of additional interest rate cuts and improved housing demand as we move forward.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/02/12/rayonier-ryn-q3-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"RYN 2025 Q3","e":"ryn","d":"2025-11-06","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Douglas Long","x":"The region should also benefit from the Section 232 tariffs on imported lumber further supporting domestic producers over time.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/02/12/rayonier-ryn-q3-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"RYN 2025 Q4","e":"ryn","d":"2026-02-12","l":"ai_spend","r":"management","s":"Mark McHugh","x":"We remain very optimistic about the long-term value creation potential from this business as substantial capital continues to flow into AI and data center infrastructure, thereby driving increased demand for clean energy solutions.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/02/12/rayonier-ryn-q4-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"RYN 2025 Q4","e":"ryn","d":"2026-02-12","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Mark McHugh","x":"So those have all been paid, but recognize there's still some costs like organizational restructuring that will phase in over time.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/02/12/rayonier-ryn-q4-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"RYN 2026 Q1","e":"ryn","d":"2026-05-07","l":"ai_spend","r":"management","s":"Mark McHugh","x":"Given the substantial capital flowing into AI and data center infrastructure, we expect solar land sales and leases to become an increasingly meaningful contributor to cash flow in the years ahead.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/06/01/rayonier-ryn-q1-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"RYN 2026 Q1","e":"ryn","d":"2026-05-07","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Mark McHugh","x":"The improvement in the lumber market to start the year reflected the impact of reduced supply due to mill curtailments and higher tariffs on Canadian imports as well as improved demand heading into the spring building season.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/06/01/rayonier-ryn-q1-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"RYN 2026 Q1","e":"ryn","d":"2026-05-07","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Mark McHugh","x":"Look, we continue to believe the U.S. lumber producers will gain market share going forward as demand improves given the duties and tariffs on imported lumber, recognizing this has been slower to materialize than we would have hoped for just given the demand environment.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/06/01/rayonier-ryn-q1-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"RYN 2026 Q1","e":"ryn","d":"2026-05-07","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Mark McHugh","x":"During this period, our average lumber price realization was $437 per MBF and shipments totaled 199 million board feet.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/06/01/rayonier-ryn-q1-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"RYN 2026 Q1","e":"ryn","d":"2026-05-07","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Mark McHugh","x":"Notably, our average lumber price realization rebounded by roughly 11% from an average of $384 per MBF in the fourth quarter for legacy PotlatchDeltic.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/06/01/rayonier-ryn-q1-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"RYN 2026 Q1","e":"ryn","d":"2026-05-07","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Mark McHugh","x":"Our leadership team has also made significant progress in optimizing our organizational structure and implementing changes that will drive meaningful overhead cost savings and operational efficiencies over time.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/06/01/rayonier-ryn-q1-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"RYN 2026 Q2","e":"ryn","d":"2026-08-06","l":"ai_spend","r":"analyst","s":"Mark Weintraub","x":"And just more generally, housing is not doing great, but we have this massive AI infrastructure build-out going on.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/08/13/rayonier-ryn-q2-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"RYN 2026 Q2","e":"ryn","d":"2026-08-06","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Mark McHugh","x":"The improvement in lumber markets during the second quarter was driven primarily by supply side factors as mill curtailments coupled with higher tariffs on Canadian imports have limited supply.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/08/13/rayonier-ryn-q2-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"RYN 2026 Q2","e":"ryn","d":"2026-08-06","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Mark McHugh","x":"My understanding is that those incremental tariffs or potential incremental tariffs on certain Canadian imports would not attach to lumber.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/08/13/rayonier-ryn-q2-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"RYN 2026 Q2","e":"ryn","d":"2026-08-06","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Mark McHugh","x":"Our average lumber price realization was $505 per MBF and shipments totaled 314 million board feet, in line with our prior guidance.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/08/13/rayonier-ryn-q2-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"RYN 2026 Q2","e":"ryn","d":"2026-08-06","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Mark McHugh","x":"Our average lumber price realization increased by roughly 18% from $427 per MBF in the first quarter, including the premerger period.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/08/13/rayonier-ryn-q2-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"RYN 2026 Q3","e":"ryn","d":"2026-11-05","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Mark McHugh","x":"The improvement in lumber markets during the third quarter was largely driven by supply-side factors, as mill curtailments, industry-wide transportation challenges, and tariffs on Canadian imports limited supply.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/11/05/rayonier-ryn-q3-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"